const e="marthoma-abu-dhabi-ss-talent-search",d=2025,n="Built from the single Talent Search 2025 rules circular. The circular prints no dates, venue, fees, contacts, registration steps or marks for judging aspects. Age is not printed; entry is by class. Judging aspects are listed without marks.",i={Title:"Rules & Criteria",Subtitle:"Mar Thoma Sunday School Abu Dhabi - Talent Search 2025",NoticeTitle:"Please Read Before Registering",Notice:"All details in the Talent Search circular replace any earlier information given.",Notes:["Each student may enter at most three individual items.","Parents are asked to stay away from the competition venues."],Sections:[{Key:"general",Title:"General rules",Items:["The purpose is to help every child develop their God-given gifts, for the glory of God, in service to fellow believers and for their own spiritual growth in the Body of Christ.","Each participant gets a chest number. Only this number is used during the event.","The NIV (New International Version) Bible is the standard version used for Bible reading.","All details in the circular about the Talent Search replace any earlier information.","Songs with their melody are listed at {{SongListLink}}."]},{Key:"eligibility",Title:"Who may enter",Items:["Each student can take part in a maximum of three individual items.","Entry is by class: Nursery (KG1 and KG2), Beginners (classes 1 and 2), Primary (3 and 4), Junior (5 and 6), Intermediate (7 and 8), Senior (9 and 10) and Young Adult (11 and 12).","Only Junior, Intermediate, Senior and Young Adult students may enter both English and Malayalam solo singing."]},{Key:"levels",Title:"Preliminary round and final",Items:["A preliminary round is held for Nursery, Beginner, Primary and Junior singing, and for Beginner and Primary storytelling. The top 12 go to the final.","Event toppers of each category can represent the Sunday School at Explore 2025."]},{Key:"judging",Title:"Judging and prizes",Items:["Judging follows the Explore rules. The decision of the judges is final.","To be considered for a prize a participant needs at least 60 percent marks. The top three are selected from each category.","If only one participant appears for an event, that participant is awarded first position."]},{Key:"conduct",Title:"Conduct",Items:["Parents are asked to stay away from competition venues to avoid distraction.","Taking videos is not allowed."]}],Documents:[{Title:"Talent Search 2025 rules",Url:"https://admtss.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/T.S-Rules-2025.pdf"}]},t=[],o=[],a=[{Title:"Preliminary Singing",Source:"Events table, General rules 4",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["The top 12 go to the final singing event."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:["Held for Nursery, Beginner, Primary and Junior."]},Markdown:`## Rules
- The top 12 go to the final singing event.

## Notes for participants
- Held for Nursery, Beginner, Primary and Junior.`},{Title:"Solo Singing",Source:"Solo singing guidelines",Sections:{About:["Solo singing is held in English and Malayalam."],TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Two songs are given for Junior, Intermediate, Senior and Young Adult. The contestant sings one song chosen by the judges.","Nursery, Beginner and Primary get only one song.","Every participant sings two stanzas (1 and 2) or two stanzas and the chorus of the given song, unless the judges say otherwise. This applies to English and Malayalam songs.","Junior, Intermediate, Senior and Young Adult follow the given notations. Nursery, Beginner and Primary have no song notations.","Valuation is separate for boys and girls from Intermediate upward.","Only Junior, Intermediate, Senior and Young Adult may enter both English and Malayalam solo singing."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:["Improvisation is not allowed in English or Malayalam solo.","Actions while singing are not allowed."],Judging:["Graded on notation, tune and melody as provided; pitch; clarity; presentation; rhythm. The first two carry greater weightage."],Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## About this competition
- Solo singing is held in English and Malayalam.

## Rules
- Two songs are given for Junior, Intermediate, Senior and Young Adult. The contestant sings one song chosen by the judges.
- Nursery, Beginner and Primary get only one song.
- Every participant sings two stanzas (1 and 2) or two stanzas and the chorus of the given song, unless the judges say otherwise. This applies to English and Malayalam songs.
- Junior, Intermediate, Senior and Young Adult follow the given notations. Nursery, Beginner and Primary have no song notations.
- Valuation is separate for boys and girls from Intermediate upward.
- Only Junior, Intermediate, Senior and Young Adult may enter both English and Malayalam solo singing.

## Not allowed
- Improvisation is not allowed in English or Malayalam solo.
- Actions while singing are not allowed.

## Judging
- Graded on notation, tune and melody as provided; pitch; clarity; presentation; rhythm. The first two carry greater weightage.`},{Title:"Preliminary Storytelling",Source:"Events table, General rules 4",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["The top 12 go to the final storytelling event."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:["Held for Beginner and Primary, in English."]},Markdown:`## Rules
- The top 12 go to the final storytelling event.

## Notes for participants
- Held for Beginner and Primary, in English.`},{Title:"Storytelling",Source:"Storytelling guidelines",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:["Maximum 3 minutes."],Rules:["The Bible passage is shared a few weeks before the event.","The Bible story may be paraphrased.","Participants memorise the story and do not dramatise it."],Allowed:["Hand movements and facial expressions."],NotAllowed:["Action or acting."],Judging:["Content: how accurately the Bible content is told as a story.","Clarity: how clearly the words are spoken, language and flow of thought.","Presentation: voice modulation, body language, eye contact, expression and hand gestures.","Moral application: how well the story ends with a message for Christian life."],Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Time and format
- Maximum 3 minutes.

## Rules
- The Bible passage is shared a few weeks before the event.
- The Bible story may be paraphrased.
- Participants memorise the story and do not dramatise it.

## Allowed
- Hand movements and facial expressions.

## Not allowed
- Action or acting.

## Judging
- Content: how accurately the Bible content is told as a story.
- Clarity: how clearly the words are spoken, language and flow of thought.
- Presentation: voice modulation, body language, eye contact, expression and hand gestures.
- Moral application: how well the story ends with a message for Christian life.`},{Title:"Colouring",Source:"Colouring guidelines",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:["Time limit 1 hour."],Rules:["The picture to colour is provided.","Each child brings their own colour pencils and drawing pad."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:["Creativity and colour harmony; neatness and precision; theme adherence; technique and skill; presentation."],Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Time and format
- Time limit 1 hour.

## Rules
- The picture to colour is provided.
- Each child brings their own colour pencils and drawing pad.

## Judging
- Creativity and colour harmony; neatness and precision; theme adherence; technique and skill; presentation.`},{Title:"Drawing",Source:"Drawing guidelines",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:["Time limit 1 hour."],Rules:["A specific Bible theme is given at the time of drawing.","The drawing sheet is provided.","Each child brings their own pencil, eraser and writing pad."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:["Creativity and originality; technical skill; composition and layout; adherence to the theme; overall impact."],Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Time and format
- Time limit 1 hour.

## Rules
- A specific Bible theme is given at the time of drawing.
- The drawing sheet is provided.
- Each child brings their own pencil, eraser and writing pad.

## Judging
- Creativity and originality; technical skill; composition and layout; adherence to the theme; overall impact.`},{Title:"Bible Reading",Source:"Bible reading guidelines",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["The portion is given at the time of reading.","The Bible is provided.","If the participant takes more than 1 minute to take the portion, or reads the portion wrongly, the participant is disqualified."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:["A podium is not allowed."],Judging:["Quickness: how quickly the portion is taken.","Accuracy: how correctly it is read.","Clarity: how clearly it is read, voice modulation.","Presentation: how the Bible is held, opened and closed, the manner of reading (without shoes, head cover for girls) and eye contact."],Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- The portion is given at the time of reading.
- The Bible is provided.
- If the participant takes more than 1 minute to take the portion, or reads the portion wrongly, the participant is disqualified.

## Not allowed
- A podium is not allowed.

## Judging
- Quickness: how quickly the portion is taken.
- Accuracy: how correctly it is read.
- Clarity: how clearly it is read, voice modulation.
- Presentation: how the Bible is held, opened and closed, the manner of reading (without shoes, head cover for girls) and eye contact.`},{Title:"Elocution",Source:"Elocution guidelines",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:["Maximum 5 minutes and minimum 2 minutes 30 seconds.","A warning bell rings after 4 minutes: 1 minute is left to conclude."],Rules:["The topic is given 15 minutes before the elocution.","If the speech is longer than 5 minutes or shorter than 2 minutes 30 seconds, the participant is disqualified."],Allowed:["Small cards with points.","Carrying the Holy Bible."],NotAllowed:["Reading the speech."],Judging:["Content: ideas on the topic, introduction, body and conclusion.","Clarity: how clearly the speech is presented, language and flow of thought.","Presentation: voice modulation, body language, eye contact, expression and hand gestures.","Moral application: how well Christian values are upheld throughout the speech."],Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Time and format
- Maximum 5 minutes and minimum 2 minutes 30 seconds.
- A warning bell rings after 4 minutes: 1 minute is left to conclude.

## Rules
- The topic is given 15 minutes before the elocution.
- If the speech is longer than 5 minutes or shorter than 2 minutes 30 seconds, the participant is disqualified.

## Allowed
- Small cards with points.
- Carrying the Holy Bible.

## Not allowed
- Reading the speech.

## Judging
- Content: ideas on the topic, introduction, body and conclusion.
- Clarity: how clearly the speech is presented, language and flow of thought.
- Presentation: voice modulation, body language, eye contact, expression and hand gestures.
- Moral application: how well Christian values are upheld throughout the speech.`},{Title:"Essay Writing",Source:"Essay writing guidelines",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:["Time limit 45 minutes.","Minimum 200 words."],Rules:["The topic is given at the time of the event."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:["Content; clarity; presentation; moral application."],Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Time and format
- Time limit 45 minutes.
- Minimum 200 words.

## Rules
- The topic is given at the time of the event.

## Judging
- Content; clarity; presentation; moral application.`}],l=[],r=[{Key:"SongListLink",Kind:"link",Label:"Song list and melodies page",Value:"https://admtss.com/talent-search/",Source:"General guidelines, Solo singing"}],s=[{Claim:"All rules, guidelines and eligibility come from the church's own Talent Search 2025 circular.",SourceType:"Primary - the event's own rules document",Source:"Mar Thoma Sunday School Abu Dhabi, Talent Search 2025 rules",Url:"https://admtss.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/T.S-Rules-2025.pdf"}],u={TemplateKey:e,Year:2025,Note:n,Page:i,ParticipantTypes:t,AgeGroups:o,Competitions:a,CompetitionAgeGroups:l,Variables:r,Evidence:s};export{o as AgeGroups,l as CompetitionAgeGroups,a as Competitions,s as Evidence,n as Note,i as Page,t as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,r as Variables,d as Year,u as default};
